L001511	\section{Details of numerical simulation}
L001512	In this appendix, we provide the details of the numerical simulation presented in the main text.
L001513	For the reader's convenience, we restate the equations to be solved:
L001514	\begin{align}
L001515	    \frac{\partial \phi^{\alpha}}{\partial t} + \frac{\partial \mathcal{J}^{\alpha}}{\partial x} = 0 \qquad \alpha=\pm,0
L001516	\end{align}
L001517	where the flux $\mathcal{J}^{\alpha}$ is given by
L001518	\begin{align}
L001519	    \mathcal{J}^{\alpha}(x,t) = \alpha c_s \phi^{\alpha} - D_{\alpha} \partial_x \phi^{\alpha} + \sum_{\beta,\gamma} G^{\alpha}_{\beta\gamma} (\phi^{\beta}\phi^{\gamma}) + \theta^{\alpha}(x,t)
L001520	\end{align}
L001521	Here, $D_{+} = D_{-} = D_s$ and the coefficient matrices $G^{\alpha}_{\beta\gamma}$ are given by Eqs.~(32) and (33) in the End Matter.
L001522	The stochastic term $\theta^{\alpha}$ represents a Gaussian white noise with correlations:
L001523	\begin{align}
L001524	    \langle \theta^{\alpha}(x,t) \theta^{\beta}(x',t')\rangle = 2 D_{\alpha} \delta_{\alpha\beta}\delta(t-t')\delta(x-x')
L001525	\end{align}
L001526	
