L001731	\subsection{Numerical verification of Eq.~(\ref{eq:appendix_modified_scaling})}
L001732	
L001733	To validate the modified scaling law Eq.~(\ref{eq:appendix_modified_scaling}), we numerically verify the theoretical prediction, $C_{\alpha} \propto 1/L$, given in Eq.~(\ref{eq:appendix_relation_C_L}).
L001734	
L001735	To this end, we focus on the correlation function at $x=0$ and $t=0$, $\Sf^\alpha_{\rm finite}(x=0, t=0)$.
L001736	For an infinite system, this quantity is exactly calculated as
L001737	\begin{align}
L001738	\Sf^\alpha_{\rm infinite}(x=0, t=0) = 1.
L001739	\end{align}
L001740	We then  obtain
L001741	\begin{align}
L001742	\Sf^\alpha_{\rm finite}(x=0, t=0) \simeq 1 - C_{\alpha}.
L001743	\end{align}
L001744	This allows $C_{\alpha}$ to be computed directly from the finite-system data:
L001745	\begin{align}
L001746	C_{\alpha} = 1 - \Sf^\alpha_{\rm finite}(x=0, t=0).
L001747	\label{eq:appendix_C_alpha_calc}
L001748	\end{align}
L001749	
L001750	In Fig.~\ref{supfig1}, we present the inverse of the correction term, $1/C_{\alpha}$, plotted as a function of the system size $L$.
L001751	The data points clearly follow a linear relationship, $1/C_{\alpha} \propto L$.
L001752	This numerical result is consistent with the theoretical prediction $C_{\alpha} \propto 1/L$ derived in Eq.~(\ref{eq:appendix_relation_C_L}), supporting the validity of the proposed finite-size correction.
